# Agent worktrees are full repo checkouts, not tracked files — never format them
.claude/worktrees/
.worktrees/

# services/web, services/marketing and lib/web-helpers are owned by biome — each has its own
# biome.json and a `format` target that runs `biome check --write`. `make format`
# routes them through that biome target, never root prettier. Prettier only reaches
# them via the husky pre-commit formatter, where it FIGHTS biome and produces CI
# `biome check` failures: prettier adds semicolons to TS (biome wants "asNeeded")
# and single-quotes CSS (biome wants double quotes). Exclude the whole packages so
# prettier never touches biome-owned code — biome is the single source of truth for
# both. (Earlier this listed only JS/TS extensions, which let prettier mangle .css.)
services/web/
services/marketing/
lib/web-helpers/

# Pre-generalization skill-behavior baseline snapshots/fixtures (BOS-249) are
# regenerated byte-for-byte by scripts/skills/skill-parity/capture-baseline.mjs
# (plain JSON.stringify(value, null, 2)). Prettier's JSON printer collapses
# short arrays onto one line, which would fight capture-baseline.test.mjs's
# determinism check (re-running the capture must reproduce the committed
# bytes exactly) every time these files are staged.
scripts/skills/skill-parity/baseline/

# The TUI proof key-vocab golden is generated by Go (tuidriver.TestKeyVocabGolden
# via json.MarshalIndent) and pinned byte-for-byte to the live namedKeys map.
# Prettier's JSON printer collapses the short "families" array onto one line,
# which MarshalIndent never does, making the committed file diverge from a fresh
# `-update` and permanently failing TestKeyVocabGolden. Go owns these bytes.
services/boss/internal/tuidriver/testdata/key-vocab.json

# The project config file and its fixtures are canonical bytes owned by
# lib/bossalib/kit/projectconfig.Encode (json.MarshalIndent style). Prettier's JSON
# printer collapses short arrays onto one line, which would break the decode ->
# encode byte-identity the format promises.
.boss-project.json
lib/bossalib/kit/projectconfig/testdata/

# The project config JSON Schema is generated from the Go types by
# projectconfig.TestSchemaGenerated (json.MarshalIndent) and pinned
# byte-for-byte; prettier would collapse its short arrays.
lib/bossalib/kit/projectconfig/schema/boss-project.schema.json

# The .boss-skills.json validator is minified ajv standalone code generated by
# scripts/skills/skill-config-schema/build.mjs and pinned byte-for-byte by its --check;
# prettier would reformat it, and it is vendored into every core's toolbox.
**/skill-config-validate.generated.mjs

# Go owns the byte-compared cross-language park verdict fixture.
lib/bossalib/attention/testdata/park_verdicts.json
